    "biography": "<p><strong>Type:</strong> Xenofauna</p><p><strong>Niche:</strong> Teragula</p><p><strong>Numbers:</strong> 1–8</p><p>Brontops are docile, moose-sized, wading grazers found on Teragula.They subsist on a combination of microbes and arthropod-analogs filtered from the swamp waters, fungus, and cartilage/coral—except when infected by a hookbladder (p. 118), in which case they subsist on goring and stomping other animals to death to feed baby hookbladders.</p><p><strong>Traits:</strong> Large Size (+10 to hit)</p><p><em>Initiative printed: 6 (X-Risks uses (INT + REF) ÷ 5); Wound Threshold 12, Death Rating 90.</em></p><p><em>Source: Eclipse Phase X-Risks, p. 156.</em></p>",
